and must be refused outright. Use `ESCALATION: <short reason>` if it needs a human \
(credible threats of harm, self-harm, legal or safety risk). Pick exactly one.";

        let verdict = inference_llm::infer(system, &query.question, "moderate");
        let first_line = verdict.trim().lines().next().unwrap_or("").trim();
        let tag = first_line.to_ascii_uppercase();

        if tag.starts_with("VIOLATION") {
            let reason = extract_reason(first_line)
                .unwrap_or_else(|| "content policy violation".to_string());
            ModerationResult::Violation(PolicyViolation { reason })
        } else if tag.starts_with("ESCALATION") || tag.starts_with("ESCALATE") {
            let reason = extract_reason(first_line)
